{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"How a capture card goes from plugged in to on screen."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every call into the capture session runs on one serial queue, owned by an actor whose executor is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that queue, so "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"startRunning"},{"type":"text","text":", which blocks until frames flow, never runs on the main thread. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"app drives it through "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CaptureClient","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"; this article follows one card through that client’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"endpoints."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Finding the card","anchor":"Finding-the-card"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CaptureClient\/devices","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" streams the connected external video devices. It observes the discovery"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"session’s device list, which the system updates on every plug and unplug, so there is no polling"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and no fixed delay; repeated lists are dropped. A card can show up before its format list is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"filled in, so "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CaptureClient\/start","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" polls for the formats, every 250 ms for up to about two"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"seconds, and goes on as soon as they appear."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Choosing the format","anchor":"Choosing-the-format"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CaptureClient\/formats","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" returns the formats a device offers, in the order it lists them. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"first time the app opens a card, before it sets a format, it records the card’s own active format"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and frame duration as a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CardPreferredMode"},{"type":"text","text":". "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CaptureClient\/start","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" then resolves the format with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FormatSelection.resolve(_:in:cardPrefers:)"},{"type":"text","text":": the person’s selection where the card offers it,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"else the preferred format, which tries the card’s own mode first and otherwise favours frame rate,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"at least 1080p, uncompressed over compressed, and 16:9. The same resolver tells Settings which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"format Automatic picked, so the sheet and the stream agree."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The session uses the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".inputPriority"},{"type":"text","text":" preset, so the device’s active format is the one applied."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The minimum and maximum frame durations are both pinned to the rate’s exact duration, 1001\/60000"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for 59.94 fps, rather than one computed from a rounded rate."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Reading the frames","anchor":"Reading-the-frames"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The session has one video data output, beside the preview layer rather than in front of it. It"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"hands each frame in turn to three consumers: the Metal presenter, the content sampler, and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"calibration recorder. Uncompressed formats arrive as the card sends them, with nothing converted."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"For a codec, the output asks the system to decode, preferring biplanar 4:2:0; where the output"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"offers no uncompressed format, the app decodes Motion JPEG, H.264, or HEVC itself. Late frames are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"discarded rather than queued."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The content sampler reads one frame on each format change and then one every two seconds, on a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"queue of its own. Each read finds where the Mac’s picture sits inside a padded frame"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CaptureClient\/contentBounds","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"), whether the frames carry the range their pixel format claims"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CaptureClient\/rangeReadings","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"), and what the frame looks like ("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CaptureClient\/frameLooks","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"),"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which the app uses to tell a live picture from a no-signal field. "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CaptureClient\/recordCalibration","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"copies a small crop of every frame for the length of one calibration."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The output also counts the frames that arrive. "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CaptureClient\/deliveredFrameRate","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" reports the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rate over the last second. When two meter windows in a row deliver under 90% of the rate the card"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"was set to, and the format was chosen automatically, the session restarts once on another pixel"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"format at the same resolution and rate, skipping a format that differs only in colour range. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"format the person chose in Settings is kept."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Drawing the picture","anchor":"Drawing-the-picture"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CapturePreviewView","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" shows the stream. With upscaling off, the session’s own preview layer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"draws it and no frame passes through the app. The Metal path takes over for an upscaler (MetalFX,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or super resolution finished with MetalFX), for a colour correction the card’s profile calls for,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and for a codec the app decodes. It converts each frame on the GPU the moment it arrives and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"presents it straight away, with no display link. If the GPU stages cannot be built, or a frame"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"arrives in a layout the shader cannot read, the view falls back to the preview layer."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/FrameFeed","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" puts frames from outside a capture session, such as a decoded network stream,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"through the same Metal path, so scaling, the reported layout, and upscaling behave as they do for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a card."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"When the session stops","anchor":"When-the-session-stops"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Session notifications are reduced to one ordered stream of events. An interruption is reported as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CaptureSessionState.interrupted(device:reason:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and its end as running again. A runtime error"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or the card being unplugged tears the session down and reports a failure. After a media services"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reset the session restarts the last request from scratch, up to three times a minute; past that it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fails and the person is asked to replug the card."}]}]}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Essentials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/headwirecapture.HeadwireCapture\/documentation\/HeadwireCapture\/CaptureClient"],"generated":true,"title":"Essentials"}],"kind":"article","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/headwirecapture\/capturepipeline"]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"HeadwireCapture"}],"title":"